// x-fix-tools-05: a labeled default that calls its own function omitting
// that label makes the CHECK diverge: each omitting site compiles the
// default, whose call is another omitting site. `--check` (and the LSP,
// which runs the same check on every edit) grows memory without bound.
// The run would recurse forever too, but the activation budget contains
// that; nothing contains the checker. Supplying the label in the inner call
// (`f(#a: 0, 1)`) checks and runs fine.
//
// command: timeout -s KILL 60 graphix --check design/review-2026-10-12/repro/x-fix-tools-05.gx
// expected: a refusal (a default that reaches itself), or exit 0, promptly
// observed: [probe] OOM-KILLED after ~12 s (6 GB cap)
let rec f = |#a = f(1), b| b;
f(1)
